# Rover P3 six-light saloon, 1948-1949.
#
# The P3 that preceded the P4: the six-light saloon with the separate
# flowing wings, the upright grille and the sloping tail. The 75's 2.1-litre
# six is the version photographed and modelled; the 60's 1.6-litre six is not
# separately represented because no 60 was photographed for the pack.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P3
#
# Dimensions 4.369 x 1.651 x 1.600 m, wheelbase 2.794 m.
#
# Shape reference: a six-light 75 in true level side elevation, with front
# and rear three-quarters and a detail view. The side view governs the wings,
# roofline and tail.
#
# Colours: no model-specific UK chart was established. Black, grey, green and
# maroon are plain names, not claimed as factory names. Weights 10, 8, 6, 6,
# total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 130 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55: an upright
# 1940s saloon with independent front suspension. Classes 2,3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1948 intro, retires staggered 1965-1968.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: PLACEHOLDER.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP3(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=10
intro_year=1948
intro_month=2
retire_year=1968
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=2,3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=55
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=413

